Kind: ablation
Issue: #977
Takes out: the disable that giving the slot back does: the function keeps its message enabled after its slot is gone, and a device that sent it would reach a vector nobody handles.  The boot's plain-MSI test reads the control word back after giving the slot back, with the enable bit still set.
Run: --edu --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: plain MSI: given back, its control word reads .* WRONG, given back and still enabled

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
index 41f66c2e..c84721d8 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/cpu/pci_msi.c
@@ -120,8 +120,7 @@ pci_msi_disarm(const struct pci_msi *m)
 {
 	if (m == 0 || m->cap == 0)
 		return;
-	msi_control_write(m, (uint16_t)(msi_control_read(m)
-					& ~PCI_MSI_CTL_ENABLE));
+	(void) msi_control_read(m);	/* 977-msi-left-enabled: given back, still enabled */
 }
 
 void
